        '0.16': 'the Wind, my child, who flung me into the ocean, Varuna\'s abode. O tamer of foes, I must give my help to Raghava.',
        '0.17': 'Rama is the best of upholders of dharma, equal to great Indra in valour.\' Hearing this from great Mainaka,',
        '0.18': 'I told the mountain of my mission, and my mind was set on going. Then I was given leave by great Mainaka.',
        '0.19': 'That great mountain then vanished, both his human form and his mountain body, into the great ocean.',
        '0.20': 'Taking up my best speed, I set out on the rest of the way, and travelled swiftly along the path for a long time.',
        '0.21': 'Then I saw the goddess Surasa, mother of the serpents; in the middle of the ocean that goddess said to me:',
        '0.22': '\'Best of monkeys, the immortals have assigned you as my food; so I shall eat you, for the gods have ordained you for me.\'',
        '0.23': 'Spoken to thus by Surasa, I stood bowed with joined palms, my face pale, and said these words:',
        '0.24': '\'The glorious Rama, son of Dasharatha, scorcher of foes, entered the Dandaka forest with his brother Lakshmana and with Sita.',
        '0.25': 'His wife Sita was carried off by the wicked Ravana. At Rama\'s command I go to her as his messenger.',
        '0.26': 'Living in his realm, good lady, you should help Rama. Or else, after seeing Maithili and Rama of tireless deeds,',
        '0.27': 'I will come back into your mouth; I promise you truly.\' When I said this to Surasa, who could take any form at will,',
        '0.28': 'she said, \'No one may pass me; this is my boon.\' Spoken to thus by Surasa, I stretched myself ten yojanas long,',
        '0.29': 'and in an instant grew half as large again; and she opened her mouth wider than my size.',
        '0.30': 'Seeing her gaping mouth, I made myself small again; at that very moment I became the size of a thumb.',
        '0.31': 'Quickly darting into her mouth, I came out again in a moment. Then the goddess Surasa, in her own form, said to me:',
        '0.32': '\'Best of monkeys, gentle one, go happily to accomplish your purpose; and unite Vaidehi with the great-souled Raghava.',
        '0.33': 'Be happy, mighty-armed monkey; I am pleased with you.\' Then all beings praised me, crying \'Well done, well done!\'',
        '0.34': 'Then I flew into the vast sky like Garuda; but my shadow was seized, and I could see nothing.',
        '0.35': 'My speed checked, I looked round in all ten directions, but saw nothing there by which my course had been stopped.',
        '0.36': 'Then the thought came to me: \'What is this obstacle that has arisen on my way, when no form is to be seen here?\'',
        '0.37': 'As I pondered, my gaze fell downward, and there I saw a fearsome rakshasi lying in the water.',
        '0.38': 'With a loud laugh that dreadful one spoke these ugly words to me as I stood there undismayed:',
