        '0.67': 'The ten-necked one, falling before the deeply grieving Sita with head bowed, said to her: "Hold me in high regard."',
        '0.68': '"Proud one, if out of arrogance you will not welcome me, then after two months, Sita, I will drink your blood."',
        '0.69': 'Hearing these words of the wicked Ravana, Sita, in great anger, gave this noble reply:',
        '0.70': '"Vilest of rakshasas! I am the wife of Rama of boundless splendour, lord of the Ikshvaku line, and the daughter-in-law of Dasharatha.',
