        '0.76': 'the noble Mandodari, and she held him back. And she spoke sweetly to him, who was tormented by desire:',
        '0.77': '"What do you want with Sita, you who equal great Indra in valour? Enjoy yourself with me today; Janaki is not better than I.',
        '0.78': 'Enjoy yourself, lord, with the maidens of the gods and gandharvas and the daughters of the yakshas; what will you do with Sita?"',
        '0.79': 'Then those women gathered together, quickly raised up the mighty night-ranger and led him away to his own palace.',
        '0.80': 'When the ten-necked one had gone, the rakshasis with their misshapen faces threatened Sita with cruel and terrible words.',
        '0.81': 'Janaki counted their words as straw; and their roaring, aimed at Sita, came to nothing.',
