        '0.125': 'suddenly rose into the sky; I seized him by the feet, whirled him round a hundred times and crushed him.',
        '0.126': 'Hearing that Aksha had gone out and been crushed, the ten-faced Ravana then, in great fury, ordered his second son, Indrajit,',
        '0.127': 'mighty and wild in battle. That whole army, and that bull among rakshasas too,',
        '0.128': 'I rendered powerless in battle and felt the greatest joy. That mighty-armed, powerful one had been sent with great confidence',
        '0.129': 'by Ravana, along with heroes wild with pride. Realizing that I was irresistible and that his own army had been crushed,',
